# Wave 2: generated source scripts S191–S291 for the posting-plan rows marked GEN-needed from D−7 to D+7
# (Oct 1–Oct 15 2026; data/content/posting_plan_90d.csv). One source script per uniqueness_group (101 groups, 606 rows).
# Written by hand to the CHARACTERS.md voice cards; no external AI calls. Same schema as scripts_runway.py, plus wave-2 keys:
#   group      the plan's uniqueness_group this script fills (tools/assign_scripts.py writes the id into those rows)
#   lane       render lane from the plan: talking_head (still + lip-sync, max 2 Veo inserts), movement (Kling Motion Control
#              from the performer clip in `clip`, production/performer/call_sheet.csv), insert (Veo/Seedance, no face,
#              voice-over only: every beat speaker ends in "-VO")
#   clip       performer clip id for movement scripts (call_sheet.csv `id`)
#   bitn       CHARACTERS.md §7 running bit number (1–24); bit names the bit. No bit repeats on a page inside 3 days.
#   grammar    grammar[0] is the plan's hook_grammar (OBJ3, IF_EVERY, MYTH_NOT, WATCH, TEST_NOW, SHARE, DEMO)
# Beats are written as (speaker, spoken, on-screen, shot) and get their time codes from the beat count (_finish below).
# Runway rows (D<0): no price, no "$", no membership talk; WAITLIST says it's free. Launch rows: BOOK states
# {{EBOOK_PRICE}} one-time; JOIN carries the full terms ("locked for as long as you stay subscribed").
# Validated by tools/build_content.py (validate_wave2) and rendered to WAVE2_SCRIPTS.md + data/content/wave2_scripts.json.
